<!-- Section 18: sec-conclusion -->
<section id="sec-conclusion" class="mx-auto mt-12 w-full max-w-4xl section-shell prose-shell scroll-mt-24">
  <h2>One Square Root, Full Understanding</h2>
  <p>One square root captures the whole idea: the altitude of a right triangle is the geometric mean of the two projections on its hypotenuse. Multiply <span set:html={rich('[[p]]')} /> and <span set:html={rich('[[q]]')} />, take the positive square root, and keep the units consistent, and the answer is in hand.</p>
  <p>Behind that short calculation sits a clean piece of geometry. The altitude creates two similar triangles, similarity gives the proportion, and the proportion gives the formula. When you can see that chain, checking answers, avoiding mistakes, and recognizing projections in new problems all become routine.</p>
</section>

